From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000007 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 17:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ingenic-sdk: motor: let devres free the device

`motor_probe()` allocates `mdev` with `devm_kzalloc()`, but the probe
error path and `motor_remove()` both call `kfree(mdev)` as well. The
device is then freed a second time when devres releases it, corrupting
the kernel heap on a failed probe and on module unload/reboot.

Drop both manual frees.

Reported in #1351 by @xu6ao2.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
--- a/4.4.94/misc/motor/motor.c
+++ b/4.4.94/misc/motor/motor.c
@@ -1005,7 +1005,6 @@
 		del_timer_sync(&motor->min_timer);
 		del_timer_sync(&motor->max_timer);
 	}
-	kfree(mdev);
 error_devm_kzalloc:
 	return ret;
 }
@@ -1056,7 +1055,6 @@
 
 	misc_deregister(&mdev->misc_dev);
 
-	kfree(mdev);
 	return 0;
 }
 
